        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(codex): bound app-server websocket handshake waits to requestTimeoutMs",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where operators using Codex app-server over websocket/unix transport would hang forever on initialize/RPC when a peer accepted the socket but never completed the WebSocket upgrade.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nBound upgrades with `ws.handshakeTimeout` **and** an explicit CONNECTING deadline at the transport chokepoint (`createWebSocketTransport`). `ws.handshakeTimeout` alone does **not** abort custom `createConnection` (Unix) upgrades — verified with a never-upgrade peer that stayed CONNECTING past the library timeout.\n\nProduction budget is resolved `appServer.requestTimeoutMs` (default 60s) from `CodexAppServerClient.start` via `resolveCodexAppServerRuntimeOptions()`.\n\n**CI / landing notes**\n- Touching `transport-websocket.ts` triggers full CodeQL `network-runtime-boundary`, which currently fails on main's unclassified `openApnsTlsTunnel` `tls.connect`. This head includes that allowlist so CI can pass; preferred split remains [#109357](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/109357).\n- Also includes the missing `pruneOrphanLocaleDocs` typings export so `check:test-types` is not blocked by current main debt (same fix as [#109364](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/109364)).\n\nCollision check: [#108795](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/108795) closed unmerged; APNs allowlist split candidate [#109357](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/109357); typings unblocker [#109364](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/109364).\n\n## User Impact\n\n- **Before:** never-upgrade peers hang initialize/RPC forever (TCP and Unix).\n- **After:** handshake follows operator `requestTimeoutMs` (default 60s) on both TCP and Unix, then emits transport exit (`1006`).\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact head: `f4fc148cf5f69f456f5df0ca14f262d09720b1cf`\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/codex/src/app-server/transport-websocket.test.ts -- --run --reporter=verbose\n```\n\n```text\n[codex handshake negative control] outcome=still-pending readyState=0 wait_ms=300 without_handshakeTimeout=true\n[codex handshake proof] timed_out=true elapsed_ms=200 code=1006 handshakeTimeout_ms=200 production_ms=60000\n[codex handshake tcp non-default] timed_out=true elapsed_ms=250 code=1006 handshakeTimeout_ms=250\n[codex handshake unix non-default] timed_out=true elapsed_ms=251 code=1006 handshakeTimeout_ms=250\n[codex handshake initialize proof] timed_out=true elapsed_ms=200 message=initialize transport failed after request write: WebSocket was closed before the connection was established\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  7 passed (7)\n```\n\n## Risk / Compatibility\n\nMedium (timeout policy). Legitimate upgrades slower than `requestTimeoutMs` now exit `1006`. CodeQL allowlist is a pre-existing APNs classification debt exposed by the transport path trigger.\n\nAI-assisted: yes (Cursor).",
